to become something real.

241
00:09:04,230 --> 00:09:05,600
But...

242
00:09:07,150 --> 00:09:10,730
That would never be okay.

243
00:09:15,270 --> 00:09:17,730
Yuki was out today, too.

244
00:09:17,730 --> 00:09:19,810
How many days is that now?

245
00:09:19,810 --> 00:09:24,560
Three? Four? I think she's been out all week.

246
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:26,770
Maybe she's sick.

247
00:09:26,770 --> 00:09:30,020
She'd text us back if she were sick.

248
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:32,520
Right, Toru?

249
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:33,850
Toru?

250
00:09:33,850 --> 00:09:35,520
Oh, sorry, what's up?

251
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:38,850
Stop spacing out! We're talking about Yuki!

252
00:09:38,850 --> 00:09:42,060
Have you gotten any texts
back from Yoshikawa- <i>san</i> ?

253
00:09:42,060 --> 00:09:47,310
Nope, she's not texting me, either.
Maybe she's dealing with family stuff.

254
00:09:47,310 --> 00:09:49,690
Huh.

255
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:53,980
We should probably tell her the test
is gonna cover different stuff now.

256
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:56,150
Oh, good idea.

257
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:59,020
How funny would it be if she
threw a tantrum over the test stuff?

258
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:01,900
I dunno if she'd throw a whole <i>tantrum</i> .

259
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:03,600
I hope she comes tomorrow.

260
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,150
Yeah.

261
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:11,230
C'mon, you need to go to school already.

262
00:10:11,230 --> 00:10:14,230
Aren't you worried about your attendance record?

263
00:10:16,650 --> 00:10:18,150
Hello? I'm talking to you!

264
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:19,940
Ow!

265
00:10:21,690 --> 00:10:24,650
This girl called Hori- <i>san</i> called.

266
00:10:24,650 --> 00:10:27,810
She said you turned off your phone.

267
00:10:27,810 --> 00:10:32,150
Lemme guess, you want something again, huh?

268
00:10:32,150 --> 00:10:36,060
Any time you want something,
you never say you want it.

269
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:38,400
I have no idea why you do this.

270
00:10:40,190 --> 00:10:45,480
There's nothing wrong or embarrassing
about wanting something.

271
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:49,850
But you need decide
if you're going to get it or not.

272
00:10:49,850 --> 00:10:53,150
You always end up
complaining about it afterwards.

273
00:10:53,150 --> 00:10:56,270
I want a hair clip like hers!

274
00:10:56,270 --> 00:11:00,270
Yuki- <i>chan</i> , you just said you didn't want one!

275
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:13,150
Here, take it.

276
00:11:13,150 --> 00:11:16,770
If you want something, then say so.

277
00:11:17,770 --> 00:11:20,850
You've had this bad habit forever.

278
00:11:22,730 --> 00:11:25,810
Hey, you stopped making those cookies, huh.

279
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:28,520
That last batch you did was pretty good.

280
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:33,810
