299
00:12:02,450 --> 00:12:04,820
out awful.

300
00:12:02,450 --> 00:12:04,820
He ate some anyways, but ended up

301
00:12:02,450 --> 00:12:04,820
in the bathroom for an hour... I feel bad!

302
00:12:07,830 --> 00:12:09,330
Kono- <i>san</i> told me she likes me.

303
00:12:19,050 --> 00:12:21,050
Kono- <i>san</i> told me she likes me.

304
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:21,060
Huh?

305
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:23,980
Huh?

306
00:12:28,940 --> 00:12:30,100
'Sup?

307
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:32,440
Yuki!

308
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:37,020
Yoshikawa's back.

309
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:40,350
Yeah. She looks good.

310
00:12:46,190 --> 00:12:50,810
Oh, yeah, did I tell you the test's
covering different stuff now?

311
00:12:50,810 --> 00:12:54,850
Yeah, I saw your text. This really sucks.

312
00:12:54,850 --> 00:12:59,400
I guess it's still all stuff
I'm crap at, though.

313
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:01,480
Yoshikawa.

314
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:03,560
Can we talk?

315
00:13:05,650 --> 00:13:07,230
Sure.

316
00:13:32,230 --> 00:13:37,770
This is probably the end
of our little game of pretend.

317
00:13:37,770 --> 00:13:39,600
What do you wanna talk about?

318
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:42,650
It's freezing up here; let's make it quick!

319
00:13:42,650 --> 00:13:46,310
I gotta give Hori her notebook back, too.

320
00:13:46,310 --> 00:13:48,020
Did you see my text?

321
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:53,350
Yeah, about Kono- <i>san</i> ?

322
00:13:53,350 --> 00:13:57,440
Yeah. When she told me she liked me...

323
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:03,520
She told me she didn't need an answer.

324
00:14:07,770 --> 00:14:09,650
What?

325
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:11,690
Wait, she doesn't?!

326
00:14:11,690 --> 00:14:13,270
Yeah.

327
00:14:13,270 --> 00:14:17,230
For some reason she thinks we're dating,

328
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:19,690
so she just wanted to get that off her chest.

329
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:26,980
Why didn't you tell her, then?
That we're not dating?

330
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:32,730
I dunno. I didn't feel like I had
to clear up the misunderstanding.

331
00:14:32,730 --> 00:14:36,810
Besides, I promised you I'd play along.

332
00:14:38,150 --> 00:14:44,020
So if you didn't have to pretend,
what would you have told her?

333
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:49,560
Please, Kono- <i>san</i> 's way out of my league.
I wouldn't be good for her.

334
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:53,730
She'll find someone way better than me.

335
00:14:57,520 --> 00:15:05,230
O-Oh. Guess that means
no more <i>sakura</i> cookies, huh.

336
00:15:05,230 --> 00:15:07,560
Yeah.

337
00:15:09,270 --> 00:15:15,980
I totally thought he'd go for her,
what with how nice she is.

338
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:20,440
You haven't made me any of those
burned cookies lately, Yoshikawa.

339
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:24,480
O-Oh, shut up. I don't burn them anymore.

340
00:15:25,940 --> 00:15:28,060
I'm a bad person.

341
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:33,900
Kono- <i>san</i> made him cookies every day,
worked up the courage to talk to him,

342
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:39,100
and told him how she felt,
even knowing she'd be rejected.

343
00:15:41,350 --> 00:15:45,100
But all I do is run away.

344
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:50,150
I'm relieved that he's not going to date her,

345
00:15:50,150 --> 00:15:52,900
but the possibility of him
not reciprocating my feelings

346
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:57,270
makes me too scared to breathe.

347
00:15:57,270 --> 00:15:59,770
Even still, I...

348
00:15:59,770 --> 00:16:02,690
I want to be the one at Toru's side.

349
00:16:06,060 --> 00:16:09,690
I'm so selfish.

350
00:16:10,690 --> 00:16:13,600
If she's warm Sakura cherry blossoms...

351
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:19,350
then I'm just gross, muddy,
freezing snow, just like my name.

352
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:27,980
I can see your breath.

353
00:16:27,980 --> 00:16:31,060
I hear today's gonna be
the coldest day of the year.

354
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:35,900
If it's gonna be this cold,
it could at least snow.

355
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:41,060
We didn't get much snow last year.
I was looking forward to some this year.

356
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:46,940
Nobody wants it to snow.

357
00:16:46,940 --> 00:16:49,520
You think so? It's so pretty, though.

358
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:54,270
Sure, it's pretty, but only in the beginning.

359
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:57,560
Shoveling it's a huge pain,
and you can slip and fall.

360
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:01,020
Yeah, I can see Miyamura slipping.

361
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,350
Yeah.

362
00:17:01,290 --> 00:17:01,750
FLOP

363
00:17:02,350 --> 00:17:09,100
And the gross muddy snow sticks
around for so long. Nobody likes <i>that</i> .

364
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:13,350
Everyone just waits for
it all to melt in the spring.

365
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:31,150
The snow doesn't melt just because it's spring.

366
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:31,980
Huh?

367
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:37,100
The snow melts because it
decides to melt on its own.

368
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:42,600
No matter how badly everyone
wants it to stick around,

369
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:47,850
the snow makes its own decision
to melt. That's why it melts.

370
00:17:47,850 --> 00:17:49,650
You got that?!

371
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:58,770
I-It melts because it gets warmer.

372
00:17:58,770 --> 00:18:04,020
So you think the snow melts
because the <i>sakura</i> blossoms ask it to?

373
00:18:06,730 --> 00:18:12,020
What is this guy talking about?

374
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:14,900
Sounds like you need to go
back to first-grade science.

375
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:17,400
E-Excuse me?!

376
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:22,310
I can't believe he can say
all that with a straight face.

377
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:26,350
Still, it makes me happy.

378
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:32,440
You're so goddamn stupid, Toru.

379
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,480
Not as stupid as you, Yoshikawa.

380
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:38,350
That's the first time you've smiled all day.

381
00:18:38,350 --> 00:18:40,600
How'd you know?

382
00:18:43,810 --> 00:18:45,980
I just know.

383
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:49,350
It's freezing out here. Let's head in.

384
00:18:49,350 --> 00:18:52,650
And whose bright idea was it
to come up here in the first place?

385
00:18:52,650 --> 00:18:54,850
Yeah, I know.

386
00:18:56,310 --> 00:18:58,520
Your hand's warm.

387
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:05,690
I really hope we get some snow!

388
00:19:05,690 --> 00:19:08,190
The pure-white kind.

389
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:15,150
Huh? You think Sakura got a boyfriend?

390
00:19:15,150 --> 00:19:21,230
Yeah, only because she
seems a lot happier as of late.

391
00:19:21,230 --> 00:19:22,310
It's the exact opposite.

392
00:19:22,310 --> 00:19:23,270
Huh?

393
00:19:23,270 --> 00:19:25,400
Okay, I'm off to tutoring!

394
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:28,310
Okay, later.

395
00:19:29,770 --> 00:19:33,900
Wait, what's the exact opposite
of getting a boyfriend?

396
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:38,020
Or was she talking about her not being happy?

397
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:39,850
Sengoku- <i>kun</i> ?

398
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:44,150
Why are you cleaning?

399
00:19:44,150 --> 00:19:47,310
The eraser bits on the floor were bothering me.

400
00:19:47,310 --> 00:19:52,310
You should let the first-years
handle that! C'mon, now.

401
00:19:52,310 --> 00:19:54,810
She's definitely in better spirits.

402
00:19:54,810 --> 00:19:57,810
Almost like a weight's off her shoulders now.

403
00:19:57,810 --> 00:20:00,690
And you should open the
window if you're going to clean.

404
00:20:00,690 --> 00:20:01,850
Where's Remi?

405
00:20:01,850 --> 00:20:04,690
She had tutoring today.

406
00:20:04,690 --> 00:20:10,810
Remi always opens the window.
That's why I forgot. Thanks.

407
00:20:12,810 --> 00:20:18,810
H-Hey, did something
change for you lately, Sakura?

408
00:20:18,810 --> 00:20:26,350
You seem happier, but I don't think it's
because something good happened...

409
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:28,690
I mean, I hope it wasn't anything, but...

410
00:20:28,690 --> 00:20:32,150
Sorry, I'm overthinking this, aren't I?

411
00:20:35,350 --> 00:20:36,650
Sakura?

412
00:20:36,650 --> 00:20:40,850
Huh? Oh, I'm heading home.
Sorry I can't help you clean.

413
00:20:40,850 --> 00:20:43,270
Hold on, Sakura!

414
00:20:47,650 --> 00:20:52,520
What... What happened?

415
00:20:53,850 --> 00:20:56,560
Nothing happened.

416
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:02,650
I got rejected before I even
had a chance to ask him out.

417
00:21:02,650 --> 00:21:08,190
That's it. That's all it is.

418
00:21:12,650 --> 00:21:17,730
What a moron. He's got to be stupid.

419
00:21:17,730 --> 00:21:21,650
Who's the idiot who didn't want to be with you?

420
00:21:21,650 --> 00:21:28,230
He should be expelled for that.

421
00:21:28,230 --> 00:21:30,310
Am I right?

422
00:21:42,560 --> 00:21:44,100
Sakura--

423
00:21:56,730 --> 00:22:02,310
That was the first time I ever saw
someone in my grade break down and sob.

424
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:13,440
It only hurts more because
nobody's in the wrong.

425
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:21,440
It started snowing.

426
00:23:48,650 --> 00:23:52,070
It May Seem Like Hate

